   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to directing the department of health to conduct a study\nrelating to the opening of a public hospital in southeast Queens; and\nproviding for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5712",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5712-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Health",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5712\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to directing the department of health to conduct a\nstudy relating to the opening of a public hospital in southeast Queens;\nand providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nDirects the department of health to conduct a study relating to opening\na new public hospital in Southeast Queens\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the department of health (DOH) to authorize and\ngather data to make recommendations to assist in facilitating the open-\ning of a public hospital in southeast Queens. Costs, possible locations,\nassociated costs, proximity to available transportation, demographics of\nthose served, socio-economic conditions, proximity to other healthcare\ninstitutions, timeline for opening, and process of opening.\n\nSection 2 allows DOH to consult all other agencies for relevant informa-\ntion\n\nSection 3 provides that DOH must submit a report to all NYS government\nleaders\n\nSection 4 provides an effective date and be deemed repealed after such\nsubmission\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSoutheast Queens has several healthcare facilities that are at times\nconstrained by capacity. Creating a new hospital in the region would\nensure effective delivery of healthcare services and maintain that resi-\ndents are served effectively.\n\nLogistically, creating a new hospital would reduce ambulatory response\ntimes, provide more beds in times of crises and generate a host of new\nhealthcare related jobs and opportunities in the region. It would be in\nthe interest of DOH to conduct such study and get a greater understand-\ning of the inherent need for a new hospital in addition to generating\nthe best available information to pinpoint a precise location in which\none can be located.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
